---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../styles/subpage.css';
import '../styles/pages/bible-course.css';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import CtaSection from '../components/ui/CtaSection.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/ui/PageHero.astro';
import SectionHeader from '../components/ui/SectionHeader.astro';
import logo from '../assets/images/thekkel-bible-course-logo.jpg';
import { ID } from '../lib/schema';
import { pad2 } from '../lib/format';

const STATS = [
  { value: '15+', label: 'Years of Excellence' },
  { value: '500+', label: 'Graduates Worldwide' },
  { value: '8', label: 'Core Disciplines' },
  { value: '100%', label: 'Online Available' },
];

const PROGRAMS = [
  {
    title: 'Old Testament Studies',
    description:
      "Comprehensive exploration of the Hebrew Scriptures with emphasis on interpretational skills, historical context, and prophetic literature. Students develop proficiency in understanding the continuity of God's redemptive plan.",
  },
  {
    title: 'New Testament Studies',
    description:
      'In-depth analysis of the New Testament writings with focus on apostolic teachings, Greek text interpretation, and the establishment of the early church. Special emphasis on Pauline epistles and prophetic books.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Systematic Theology',
    description:
      "Dispensational theology with special emphasis on the distinctives of the Plymouth Brethren Movement. Students examine major doctrines through a biblical framework, understanding God's progressive revelation.",
  },
];

const COURSES = [
  {
    title: 'Philosophy',
    description: 'Christian philosophical thought and worldview development through biblical lens',
  },
  { title: 'Church History', description: 'Historical development of Christianity from apostolic age to modern times' },
  {
    title: 'Sociology & Psychology',
    description: 'Understanding human behavior and society from a biblical perspective',
  },
  { title: 'World Missions', description: 'Biblical foundations and contemporary strategies for global evangelism' },
  { title: 'Economics', description: 'Biblical principles of stewardship and understanding economic systems' },
  { title: 'World Religions', description: 'Comparative study of major world religions from a Christian perspective' },
  { title: 'Apologetics', description: 'Defending the Christian faith in contemporary intellectual contexts' },
  { title: 'Biblical Languages', description: 'Introduction to Hebrew and Greek for enhanced biblical exegesis' },
];

const description =
  'The Thekkel Online Bible Course with Dr. Sunny Ezhumattoor: Old and New Testament studies, dispensational systematic theology, apologetics, church history and more, taught entirely online.';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Thekkel Online Bible Course | Narrow Path Ministries"
  {description}
  path="/bible-course.html"
  crumbs={[{ name: 'Bible Course', path: '/bible-course.html' }]}
  mainEntity={{
    '@type': 'Course',
    name: 'Thekkel Online Bible Course',
    description,
    provider: { '@id': ID.organization },
    instructor: { '@id': ID.founder },
    inLanguage: 'en',
  }}
>
  <PageHero
    title="Thekkel Online"
    highlight="Bible Course"
    subtitle="Comprehensive Theological Education for the Twenty-First Century"
  >
    <div class="hero-logo">
      <!-- Served at its native 320×282 so the rendered height (176.25px at 200px wide) matches exactly. -->
      <Image src={logo} alt="Thekkel Home Bible Course Logo" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" />
    </div>
  </PageHero>

  <section class="college-intro">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="college-badge fade-in">
        <div class="college-name">THEKKEL</div>
        <div class="college-motto">Rightly Dividing the Word of Truth</div>
      </div>

      <p class="intro-text fade-in">
        The Online Bible Course with Dr. Sunny Ezhumattoor exists to serve and equip the Church for the twenty-first
        century. We provide students with exceptional interpretational skills in Old and New Testament studies,
        alongside fundamental knowledge in philosophy, history, sociology, psychology, world missions, theology,
        economics, world religions, and apologetics.
      </p>

      <p class="intro-text fade-in">
        Our holistic curriculum challenges and prepares students to display sound reasoning, communicate clearly, and
        demonstrate effective research skills while developing their complete Christian character. Dr. Ezhumattoor's
        teaching approach encompasses not only biblical knowledge but also personality development, spiritual formation,
        moral character building, and practical life skills essential for effective Christian living.
      </p>

      <p class="intro-text fade-in">
        The goal of all instruction is to foster intellectual, spiritual, and personal growth as students engage deeply
        with Scripture and seek to glorify God in all aspects of life. Through comprehensive mentorship, students
        receive guidance in developing Christ-like character, effective communication, leadership qualities, and the
        practical wisdom needed to navigate life's challenges as mature believers.
      </p>

      <p class="intro-text fade-in">
        Through personalized online learning, students receive comprehensive biblical education that combines academic
        rigor with complete character development, preparing them to serve effectively in their communities and callings
        as well-rounded Christian leaders and disciples.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="stats-bar">
    <div class="stats-container">
      {STATS.map((s) => (
        <div class="stat-item fade-in">
          <span class="stat-value">{s.value}</span>
          <span class="stat-label">{s.label}</span>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="programs-section">
    <div class="container">
      <SectionHeader
        label="Academic Programs"
        title="Areas of Study"
        subtitle="Comprehensive biblical and theological education rooted in dispensational theology"
      />

      <div class="programs-grid">
        {PROGRAMS.map((p, i) => (
          <div class="program-card fade-in">
            <div class="program-number">{pad2(i + 1)}</div>
            <h3 class="program-title">{p.title}</h3>
            <p class="program-description">{p.description}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="curriculum-section">
    <div class="container">
      <SectionHeader
        label="Core Curriculum"
        title="Foundational Courses"
        subtitle="Interdisciplinary approach to theological education"
      />

      <div class="curriculum-grid">
        {COURSES.map((c) => (
          <div class="course-card fade-in">
            <h3 class="course-title">{c.title}</h3>
            <p class="course-description">{c.description}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="faculty-section">
    <div class="container">
      <SectionHeader
        label="Ministry Philosophy"
        title="Finding the Balance: A Two-Pronged Approach"
        subtitle="Building a Church That Reaches Out and Grows Within"
      />

      <div class="faculty-highlight fade-in">
        <p class="faculty-quote">
          Successful church ministry thrives on a sacred balance — between outreach and in-reach. We are called not only
          to go into the world and share the Gospel, but also to nurture and strengthen the faith of those already
          within our fellowship. Outreach is the hand of the Church extended to the world; in-reach is the heart of the
          Church beating for its members.
        </p>
        <p class="faculty-quote faculty-quote-follow">
          These two aspects are not in competition but in harmony. A church that reaches outward without caring inward
          may draw crowds but lose connection. One that looks only inward risks becoming isolated and ineffective. True
          ministry finds its strength where compassion for the lost meets care for the found — a rhythm of service that
          reflects the heart of Christ Himself.
        </p>
        <div class="explore-further">
          <p class="explore-further-title">Explore Further:</p>
          <p class="explore-further-text">
            Read the Bible Course Materials and Previous Session Notes to learn more about how in-reach ministry
            strengthens the Church community, deepens discipleship, and sustains lasting spiritual growth.
          </p>
          <div class="explore-further-action">
            <a href="/integrity-values.html" class="btn-read-materials">
              <span>Read the materials here</span>
              <svg
                width="20"
                height="20"
                viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                fill="none"
                stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="2"
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                aria-hidden="true"
              >
                <path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"></path>
              </svg>
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaSection
    title="Begin Your Theological Journey"
    text="Join students worldwide who are being equipped for effective ministry through comprehensive biblical education."
  >
    <p class="cta-note">For online study visit: www.thekkel.com</p>
    <div class="cta-actions">
      <a href="#contact" class="btn btn-white">
        Apply Now
      </a>
      <a href="/about.html" class="btn btn-secondary">
        Learn More About Dr. Sunny
      </a>
    </div>
  </CtaSection>
</BaseLayout>
